EARLIER ATTEMPTS AND FOLLOW-UP
Attempt 1: ARM64 full suite failed in the initial advertisement of the previous RPKI regression (export/disable, rpki_revalidation_test.go:178), before any RPKI mutation. Investigation found a reproducible initial-replay/state-publication gap; a deterministic regression was added and the production state ordering corrected (issue #11). A direct attribution of every internal detail of that first failure is not claimed.
Attempt 2: ARM64 full race suite passed; the GR reconnect fixture failed because its TCP connection was accepted while the peer remained Idle and was closed before OPEN completed. The fixture now retries an EOF during the handshake, like an active peer, while still rejecting NOTIFICATION errors.

Attempt 3: the current full ARM64 race suite and 1000 repetitions passed; the older VRF TCP fixture had the same EOF-in-Idle handshake failure. The shared connect helper now retries the full handshake on EOF/OSError and fails on NOTIFICATION. Final protocol validation below runs all nine scenarios three times.

